- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/oceanevaluate.html
- Summary (EN): Converts the layers of an Ocean Spectrum COP into an animated ocean surface. It evaluates them at a given time to produce the surface height and horizontal displacement.
- Résumé (FR) : Transforme les couches d'un spectre d'océan en surface animée, en donnant la hauteur et le déplacement horizontal à un instant donné, avec une taille d'océan qui doit correspondre au spectre.

- Inputs meaning: ["amplitude: the amplitude layer from an Ocean Spectrum COP", "frequency: the frequency layer from an Ocean Spectrum COP", "phase: the phase layer from an Ocean Spectrum COP"]

- Key parameters: ["Scale: overall multiplier on wave amplitude; higher values produce taller waves", "Chop: sharpens wave crests and flattens troughs by pushing the surface toward the peaks", "Time: the time at which the ocean surface is evaluated", "Ocean Size: world-space size of the input spectrum; should match the Ocean Size of the Ocean Spectrum COP", "Outputs: height (vertical surface height), cusp (wave peak sharpness), dir (horizontal displacement, which can distort textures such as foam through the Distort COP)"]

- Caveats: ["The page has no separate warning section. If Ocean Size does not match the Ocean Spectrum COP, the horizontal displacement is scaled incorrectly."]

